Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: keep capture buffers across encoder drain

Capture buffers can be requeued after firmware completes EOS but
before userspace dequeues LAST. Returning them empty in STOPPED
leaves empty completions with zero timestamps after START. This
breaks frame reconciliation.

Keep capture buffers on the normal firmware queue across drain
and restart. This fixes a hardware regression that queues capture
after LAST before START; it previously returned an empty non-LAST
buffer as the next encoded frame.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1353,7 +1353,9 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 
-	if (inst->enc_state == VENUS_ENC_STATE_STOPPED) {
+	/* Capture buffers queued after EOS are needed when encoding resumes. */
+	if (inst->enc_state == VENUS_ENC_STATE_STOPPED &&
+	    V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vb->type)) {
 		vbuf->sequence = inst->sequence_cap++;
 		vbuf->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 		vb2_set_plane_payload(vb, 0, 0);
